# Managed by uav_ansible — stable name for the GNSS PPS input.
# /dev/ppsN numbering is not stable on this board: the L4T kernel builds in the
# "ktimer" test source (CONFIG_PPS_CLIENT_KTIMER=y), which takes pps0 at every
# boot and ticks off a kernel timer, not a real edge; igc adds the i226 PHC as
# another PPS source when it loads. Name the pps-gpio one instead.
#
# By its name attribute, the only handle it has: pps-gpio registers its source
# without a parent device (/devices/virtual/pps/ppsN), so DRIVERS=="pps-gpio"
# matches nothing. It names the source "<platform device>.<id>": a platform
# device created from the device tree is named after its node and gets id -1
# (PLATFORM_DEVID_NONE), so the overlay's root-level node "pps"
# (pps-gpio.dts.j2) becomes "pps.-1". A root node name is unique, so this
# cannot match anything else; rename the node and this must follow.
SUBSYSTEM=="pps", ATTR{name}=="pps.-1", SYMLINK+="{{ pps_device | basename }}"
